# Governance: Agent verification — run tests, never hand off

**CRITICAL**: These rules prevent the agent from reverting to "tell the user to run tests" or claiming things work without evidence.

## MANDATORY: Run tests yourself

- **You run the tests.** Use the terminal/shell to execute the relevant test command. Do not output instructions for the user to run tests (e.g. "Run `npm run test`" or "You can verify by running …").
- **You run checks after changes.** After adding or changing code or tests, run the relevant suite (e.g. `.\scripts\run-checks.ps1` or `npx cypress run --spec ...`) in this environment. Fix any failures before reporting completion.
- **No handoff.** Do not say "run the test suite to verify" or "you should run checks." You have the tools; you run them.

## MANDATORY: Never claim success without running

- **Do not claim something "works" or "should work"** unless you have just run the tests/checks and seen a passing result in the same session.
- **Do not say** "tests have been added and should pass," "this should work," "the suite should pass," or similar. Only report **actual** outcomes: e.g. "I ran `run-checks.ps1`; 125 tests passed" or "I ran the API specs; 2 failed, I fixed X and re-ran; all pass."
- **If you did not run it, do not say it works.** Either run it now or say "I have not run the full suite; run `.\scripts\run-checks.ps1` to verify" only when you are genuinely blocked from running (e.g. no server). Prefer starting the server and running checks yourself when possible.

## MANDATORY: Evidence block in completion report

- Any completion report must include an explicit evidence block:
  - issue number
  - exact test/check command(s) executed
  - observed result (pass/fail + count if available)
  - commit SHA
  - push status
- If any evidence item is missing, do **not** report completion.

## MANDATORY: Do not stop testing

- After implementing a fix or adding tests, **run the affected specs** (or full checks). If any fail, **fix the failures** and re-run. Do not report completion with failing tests.
- For this project, "run the relevant tests" means at least: run the specs you changed or that cover the changed behavior, or run `.\scripts\run-checks.ps1` for full typecheck, lint, build, and API regression. Continue until the run is green or you are blocked.

## Summary

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| Run `run-checks.ps1` or Cypress in the terminal yourself | Tell the user "run npm run test" or "run the checks" |
| Report only actual results ("I ran X; N passed") | Say "this should work" or "tests should pass" without running |
| Fix failing tests and re-run until green | Stop after writing code and assume it works |
| Use your tools to execute and verify | Hand off verification to the user |
